# The owner approves every change to code that is deployed to AWS
# (Carsten, 2026-11-13, NOC-272): the paths that .github/workflows/relay-deploy.yml
# builds and deploys from, and this file. Branch protection requires a code
# owner's review on main (docs/relay-deploy.md). scripts/relay-deploy-workflow.test.mjs
# keeps these paths equal to the workflow's, and the workflow's to every
# workspace crate the function links.
#
# The crates' tests/ directories are not part of the deployed build, so they
# need no owner review (Carsten, 2026-11-20, NOC-403); src/ stays owned,
# inline #[cfg(test)] modules included. GitHub takes the last pattern that
# matches, and a pattern with no owner leaves its path unowned (`!` does not
# work here). So each test directory is listed again, without an owner, after
# the line that owns its crate. The workflow excludes the same directories.

